[[File:BadBatchLineup-SWquiz.png|thumb|right|300px|Clone Force 99 consisted of five CT-99 clones: Hunter, Wrecker, Tech, Echo, and Crosshair, each had an enhanced skill set to serve the Galactic Republic.]]
{{Dialogue|Hunter|We're clones. Same as you.|Deke|You don't look like clones.|Stak|They must be 99s. Defectives.|Wrecker|Defective and effective.|attr=Deke and Stak meet the Bad Batch|src=<ref name="Paths Unknown">{{TBB|Paths Unknown}}</ref>}}
'''Genetically defective clones''',<ref name="TBB:AM">{{TBB|Aftermath (episode)}}</ref> designated as '''CT-99s''',<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref> nicknamed as '''Bad Batchers''',<ref name="Clone Cadets">{{TCW|Clone Cadets}}</ref> also referred to as '''99s''' and '''defective CTs'''<ref name="Paths Unknown" /> or alternatively known as '''defective clone troopers''' ('''DCTs'''),<ref name="DRVG">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> were [[clone trooper]]s who had altered [[gene]]s due to extensive experimentation<ref name="Secrets of the Clone Troopers">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Clone Troopers]]''</ref> or as a result of the [[cloning]] process.<ref name="TBB:AM" /> While the physically impaired [[Clone 99]] was relegated to the tasks of a [[maintenance duty clone]],<ref name="Clone Cadets" /> the members of [[Clone Force 99]]&mdash;[[Clone Sergeant]] [[Hunter]], [[Wrecker]], [[Tech]], and [[Crosshair]]&mdash;possessed unique mutations that allowed them to be specialist [[soldier]]s<ref name="TBB:AM" /> in the [[Special Operations Brigade]],<ref name="French Encyclopedia">{{EncyclopediaCite|Din Djarin and Other Characters of the Underworld}}</ref> [[Echo]] may not have been born different, like the rest of the batch, but after the changes he went through, Echo became a natural addition to their ranks,<ref name="Secrets of the Clone Troopers" /> as a CT-99 member,<ref name="War-Mantle" /> each member of the Batch had a unique genetic mutation designed to heighten a specific skill set,<ref name="Secrets of the Clone Troopers" /> to serve the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. Due to the genetic mutations of the Bad Batch affecting their [[Behavioral modification biochip|inhibitor chips]], they were not obliged to abide by [[Order 66]], issued by [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] at the end of the war so that the clones of the [[Galactic Republic]] would [[Great Jedi Purge|kill]] their [[Jedi]] commanders. Nevertheless, Crosshair chose to follow orders and be loyal to the [[Galactic Empire]] that [[Proclamation of the New Order|succeeded]] the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="TBB:AM" />

[[Muzzle]] was a defective clone who served as an [[Advanced Recon Commando]] and later [[Desertion|deserted]] the Republic to secretly lead the [[Aurodium Sword]], a [[company]] of [[Mercenary|mercenaries]], during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Collapse">''[[Collapse of the Republic]]''</ref> Defying the Empire, the other members of Clone Force 99 [[Extraction on Daro|extracted]] the clone deserter [[Gregor]] from an [[Imperial Base on Daro|Imperial base]] on [[Daro]]. Gregor initially assumed that they were [[clone commando]]s like him until Hunter identified his [[squad]] as CT-99s, indicating that they were genetically defective clones.<ref name="War-Mantle" />

